# Response headers for the whole site, in the format Cloudflare Pages reads.
# The API server applies this same file when it serves the build itself
# (STATIC_DIR, backend/static.go), so these are the site's headers wherever
# it runs: change them here and nowhere else. backend/static_test.go and
# src/pwa/headers.test.ts check what they must say.
#
# The app runs only its own script and talks only to its own server. React
# Native for Web writes the app's styles into <style> tags as it draws, so
# inline styles are allowed (Edwin, 2026-10-27); inline scripts never are. The read pages run no script at all; when ads come they get their
# own rule here, and nothing changes for the app.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), browsing-topics=(), publickey-credentials-get=(self), publickey-credentials-create=(self)
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Built files carry their content's hash in their names, so they never change.
/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/_expo/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The public read pages: plain pages with their styles inline and no script.
/read/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
